  "prefLabel": "Pod 401.05 Reinstatement of License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pod 401.05 Reinstatement of License.\n\n(a) Any applicant whose license has expired for more than one year and who wishes to obtain a license shall apply for initial licensure as provided in Plc 304.\n\n(b) Applicants applying for licensure pursuant to (a) above shall provide proof of completion of continuing education for the 2 years immediately preceding the date of application which meets the requirements of Pod 402.\n\n(c) Applicants for reinstatement shall pay the reinstatement fee specified in Plc 1002.40.\n\nSource. #9901-A, eff 4-15-11, (paras (a) & (c)); amd by #9901-B, eff 4-15-11, (para (b), EXPIRED: 4-15-19 in (paras (a) & (c)); ss by #12811, INTERIM, eff 6-14-19, EXPIRED: 12-11-19\n\nNew. #13819, eff 2-9-24; ss by #14457, eff 2-8-26, EXPIRES: 2-8-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pod100-500.html"
